      "problem": "Solve $f(x)=0,$ where $f(x) = \\dfrac{x+1}{x^2-x-2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{x+1}{{x}^{2}-x-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+1}{(x+1)(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(x+1)}}{\\cancel{(x+1)}(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the numerator equal to zero, we get $1=0,$ which is a false statement. Therefore, $f(x)=0$ has no solution.",
